Subject: cmake: PD_VERSION_BRANCH, so the boot screen names DarkPad

DarkPad overlay 0091. The legal screen shows "Perfect Dark (VERSION_BRANCH)"
(title.c). VERSION_BRANCH is the git branch of CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR, which for
build/src is the port checkout, so a working branch such as
codex/readme-icon-controller-default ran off the screen. build-ios.sh passes
PD_VERSION_BRANCH=DarkPad. Unset, the build is exactly upstream.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -177,6 +177,15 @@
   set(VERSION_BRANCH "port-custom")
 endif()
 
+# PD_VERSION_BRANCH (DarkPad overlay 0091): the name the title's legal screen
+# shows as "Perfect Dark (<branch>)" and the log's version line. build/src has
+# no .git, so the rev-parse above answers with the port checkout's branch -
+# a long working-branch name ran off the boot screen. Netplay compares
+# VERSION_HASH only (0083), never the branch.
+if(DEFINED PD_VERSION_BRANCH AND NOT PD_VERSION_BRANCH STREQUAL "")
+  set(VERSION_BRANCH "${PD_VERSION_BRANCH}")
+endif()
+
 message(STATUS "Version: ${VERSION_ROMID}, hash ${VERSION_HASH}, branch ${VERSION_BRANCH}")
 
 configure_file("${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/port/include/versioninfo.h.in" "${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/port/include/versioninfo.h" @ONLY)
